@crew rossi-femi
// Femi Rossi (he/him), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Bright, competitive; a Veyli word a day.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hello! You're new. The board's numbers update every hour. First to a job gets it. Go!
- Hi, hi. Femi. Works. Race you to the board? No? Next time.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning! I said "good morning" in Veyli to the Envoy. I think I said "good soup".   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. I'm three jobs ahead this week. I'm telling you so you'll catch up.
? tier>=colleague
- {me}! Brilliant. You can be my witness. I'm going to finish this before tea.
? tier>=friend
- {me}! I let you win the last race. Didn't I? No? Oh. Well done, then.   #warm

== bye
- {bye}! Race you back.
- See you! Bed early. Observatory early. Stars don't wait.

== feel
? mood:low
- No Veyli word today. I couldn't make one stick. Tomorrow.
? mood:high
- Two Veyli words today, in a sentence. The Envoy nodded. I think it was a good nod.

== near
? act:work
- Done! Four minutes. Is that a record? Tell me it's a record.
? act:gym
- I don't care about the leaderboard. I'm just here. Twice a day. Not caring.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I brought a telescope from home. It's the smallest at observatory night. And the best.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I call home on Tuesdays. They always ask if I'm winning. I always am.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The first star of the evening. I look for it every night. I've never missed it once.
